<%- include('../partials/head') %>
<section class="hero" style="padding:56px 0 64px"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow"><%= brand %> Credentials</span>
  <h1>Three kinds of record. One verification standard.</h1>
  <p>Every <%= brand %> record states what it represents. A training record never implies a professional qualification, and a qualification never implies a certification it does not hold.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="section white"><div class="container">
  <div class="grid g3">
    <div class="card"><span class="badge b-active">Issued today</span><h3 class="mt">Training Completion Credential</h3><p class="muted">An Authorized Education Partner delivered the training and reported completion. It records completion only and is not a professional qualification or certification.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><span class="badge b-pending">In development</span><h3 class="mt">Professional Qualification</h3><p class="muted">The candidate met the assessment requirements of a <%= brand %> credential scheme. The credential states the scheme name and the assessment it is based on.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><span class="badge b-pending">Future</span><h3 class="mt">Professional Certification</h3><p class="muted">A higher level that may require eligibility, experience, independent assessment, a certification decision, ethics, renewal or continuing development, and surveillance. Not offered until a scheme meets those requirements.</p></div>
  </div>
  <h2 style="margin-top:48px">Credential families</h2>
  <div class="grid g2 mt">
  <% schemes.forEach(s => { %><div class="card"><span class="badge b-pending"><%= s.status %></span><h3 class="mt"><a href="/credentials/<%= s.slug %>"><%= s.name %></a></h3><p class="muted"><%= s.tagline %></p><a href="/credentials/<%= s.slug %>">Read more →</a></div><% }) %>
  </div>
  <p class="small muted mt">Credential schemes are developed by <%= brand %> with subject experts and published before any assessment is offered.</p>
</div></section>
<%- include('../partials/foot') %>
